    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle given its vertices \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given coordinates \\((x_1, y_1) = (0, 0)\\), \\((x_2, y_2) = (0, 5)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3) = (7, 12)\\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0(5 - 12) + 0(12 - 0) + 7(0 - 5) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSimplifying inside the absolute value:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 0 + 7(-5) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -35 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 35 = 17.5\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the triangle is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.\n\nAlternatively, we can also use the coordinates to determine the height and base of the triangle and calculate the area directly. The base of the triangle is the horizontal distance between \\((0,0)\\) and \\((0,5)\\), which is 5 units. The height of the triangle is the vertical distance from \\((7,12)\\) to the line \\(y = 5\\), which is \\(12 - 5 = 7\\) units. Thus, the area is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 7 = 17.5\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the area of the triangle is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.",
